WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.162 --> 00:00:06.196
Fashinza connects fashion brands with verified garment factories. Here is the whole process, start to finish.

2
00:00:06.196 --> 00:00:10.612
Brands and manufacturers each have their own way in. We'll start as a fashion brand.

3
00:00:10.612 --> 00:00:17.882
Registration is free. The brand enters its name, company and work email.

4
00:00:17.882 --> 00:00:21.591
A short company profile comes next.

5
00:00:21.591 --> 00:00:24.476
The dashboard shows what to do next: create a production project.

6
00:00:24.476 --> 00:00:31.249
The project wizard collects everything a factory needs, one step at a time. Drafts are saved at every step.

7
00:00:31.249 --> 00:00:36.677
Specifications: fabric, colours, sizes and the processes the garment needs.

8
00:00:36.677 --> 00:00:39.673
Quantity, target price and delivery date.

9
00:00:39.673 --> 00:00:42.177
Certifications can be made mandatory. Here the brand requires GOTS.

10
00:00:42.177 --> 00:00:44.744
Samples are requested by default. The brand asks for a size M fit sample.

11
00:00:44.744 --> 00:00:48.558
The tech pack is required. Measurement charts and reference images can be added too.

12
00:00:48.558 --> 00:00:51.261
A final check, then the brief is submitted for matching.

13
00:00:51.261 --> 00:00:59.690
Matching follows published rules. Only verified factories that fit the order are invited, and the reasons are shown.

14
00:00:59.690 --> 00:01:03.535
Now we're the matched factory. The new project appears under Opportunities.

15
00:01:03.535 --> 00:01:06.123
The factory can see exactly why it was matched.

16
00:01:06.123 --> 00:01:13.797
The quotation is itemised. Fashinza calculates the total on the server.

17
00:01:13.797 --> 00:01:19.551
The quotation is sent. The brand is notified.

18
00:01:19.551 --> 00:01:23.820
Quotations are compared side by side: price, minimum order, production time and sampling.

19
00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:30.184
Accepting creates the order. Production follows eight milestones, from fabric sourcing to delivery.

20
00:01:30.184 --> 00:01:34.886
Each stage is completed with evidence, such as a fabric invoice or swatch photo.

21
00:01:34.886 --> 00:01:42.117
Then the factory submits a sample with photos.

22
00:01:42.117 --> 00:01:45.069
The brand reviews the sample. It can ask for changes, or approve it.

23
00:01:45.069 --> 00:01:50.966
Approval starts bulk production, and the first milestone payment falls due.

24
00:01:50.966 --> 00:01:59.908
Cutting, stitching and finishing are each completed with photos. Both sides see the same progress.

25
00:01:59.908 --> 00:02:04.851
Quality inspection follows ISO 2859-1 AQL sampling. The plan says how many garments to inspect.

26
00:02:04.851 --> 00:02:10.450
A passed inspection waits for the brand. A failed one would send the batch back for rework.

27
00:02:10.450 --> 00:02:13.349
The brand accepts the inspection report.

28
00:02:13.349 --> 00:02:18.510
Payments fall due as milestones are approved. This demo uses the sandbox, so no real money moves.

29
00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:23.948
The payment provider confirms the charge, and the milestone is marked paid.

30
00:02:23.948 --> 00:02:31.431
The factory records the carrier and tracking number when the goods ship.

31
00:02:31.431 --> 00:02:34.433
The brand confirms the goods arrived, which completes the order.

32
00:02:34.433 --> 00:02:37.636
Delivered. Every step, file and decision stays in the order's history.

33
00:02:37.636 --> 00:02:41.036
Ready to start? Register free as a fashion brand or as a manufacturer.
